With --disable-background-networking, defer only policy-owned listener startup
until its CloudPolicyCore has a registered client. Observe existing core/client
lifecycle seams: a late connection or registration starts the listener exactly
once; a disconnect drops the soon-to-be-destroyed client observation but keeps
the core observation for managed reconnect. Core destruction clears deferred
observations and the raw core reference. Shutdown detaches observations and
does not shut down a listener that never started. No Profile pointer is added.

After startup, leave invalidation delivery, token renewal, uploads and retries
unchanged, including managed reconnect. Without the flag, retain eager startup.
No changes to profile invalidation providers, GCM, InstanceID, explicit webpage
Push, authentication, cookies, native forms, TLS or security policy consumers.

Source route: eager UserFmRegistrationTokenUploader profile initialization
creates policy/remote-command FmRegistrationTokenUploaders. Their listener
Start() fetches a lazy InstanceID token, but InstanceIDImpl construction calls
GetInstanceIDData(), whose desktop implementation requests IMMEDIATE_START.
InstanceIDImpl also discards GetToken flags. This is source attribution, not
proof that this route caused the observed android.clients.google.com checkin.

Add seven desktop lifecycle regressions in both flag modes using the real
InvalidationListener, InstanceIDDriver and InstanceIDImpl over the existing
fake GCM transport. Count actual store reads and token fetches; assert handler
presence and upload calls. Cover unregistered startup, existing/late managed
registration, duplicate notifications, reconnect before registration, managed
token renewal after reconnect, shutdown before later registration, and pending
token delivery after shutdown. Also cover core destruction while deferred.

Test target: unit_tests
Test filter: FmRegistrationTokenUploaderTest.*:BackgroundNetworking/FmRegistrationTokenUploaderLifecycleTest.*
New real-driver lifecycle tests exclude Android, whose InstanceID backend is
different; the implementation and existing tests remain cross-platform.
Add explicit non_code_constants dependency to policy impl and tests, and real
invalidation/GCM test-support dependencies to policy unit_tests. No new library.
No compilation, tests, formatters, linters or patch-application checks run.

